<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tbx style="dca" type="TBX-Basic" xml:lang="en" xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:30042:ed-2">
  <tbxHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <source>https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0138</source>
    </fileDesc>
  </tbxHeader>
  <text>
    <body>
      <conceptEntry id="dpp-0138">
      <languageSection xml:lang="eng">
          <descrip type="definition">
            <p>salted cryptographic commitment to the parent, recorded in the child's event log, by which a child satisfies the bidirectional parent-knowledge requirement without disclosing the identity of the parent</p>
          </descrip>
          <note type="note">Proof of binding is distinct from knowledge of parent: verifiable modes establish that the child is validly installed in some parent under a given profile (warranty, compliance) without revealing which parent; full disclosure occurs only by ceremony.</note>
          <note type="note">An optional escrow envelope under a threshold trustee (concept dpp-0137) accompanies the commitment where future disclosure must remain possible.</note>
      </languageSection>
      </conceptEntry>
    </body>
  </text>
</tbx>
